# Back / navigate-up control (unified)

Use this pattern for **icon-only “back”** links or buttons that sit **before a page title** (toolbar, editor headers, etc.). Brand UI uses Tailwind `primary` (green/teal from `tailwind.config.js`).

## Markup

- **`router-link`** when navigating in-app; **`button`** when using `router.back()` or similar.
- **Square**: `h-8 w-8` (compact; use `h-9 w-9` only if a touch target needs to be larger on a specific screen).
- **Chevron**: Heroicons-style `M15 19l-7-7 7-7` in `h-4 w-4`, plus **`rtl:rotate-180`** on the SVG so “back” points the right way in Arabic.
- Always set **`aria-label`** to a translated string (e.g. “Back to …”), not visible text.

## Classes (copy as one line or wrap; keep together)

```
inline-flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-primary-200/80 bg-primary-100 text-primary-700 shadow-sm hover:border-primary-300 hover:bg-primary-200 hover:text-primary-800 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary-500/40 focus-visible:ring-offset-2
```

(`router-link` and `<button>` both support these classes.)

## Do not

- Do not use neutral **gray-only** fills for this control unless the design explicitly deprecates brand tint.
- Do not omit **`aria-label`** on icon-only controls.

When adding new back/up affordances in `school-management-unified`, **reuse this styling** unless a mockup says otherwise.
